<!-- .dockerignore (A1). It lists what Docker must not copy into the image.

It keeps secrets and local state out: .env, *.db, logs and mlruns.
It leaves out tests, docs, notebooks and models, because the image doesn't serve from them. models is excluded because the weights come from fetch_model.py.
It excludes data/* but keeps data/reference, because the drift detector needs the reference snapshot at runtime.
A smaller build context also builds faster. -->

# Keep the build context small and keep secrets and local state out of the image.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# Local state
.env
.env.*
*.db
*.sqlite
mlruns
mlartifacts
logs

# Not needed to serve predictions
tests
docs
notebooks
models
data/*
!data/reference
*.zip
